'''Fireball''' is a level 10 Fire [[mage]] ability.

==Trivia==
* Fireball is...
**One of the [[Warlock (Warcraft I)|Warlock]]'s abilities in ''[[Warcraft: Orcs & Humans]]''. Its description in the [[Warcraft: Orcs & Humans manual|game manual]] reads: ''"The basic fire spell which all followers of the Orcish cults (the underworld) first learn. It channels the flames of Hades through the caster's body, allowing the wielder to direct it as a missile at anyone he chooses. It is a dangerous magik to employ, but the effects seem to delight even the lowest circle of Warlock to no end."''
**One of the [[Mage (Warcraft II)|Mage]]'s abilities in ''[[Warcraft II]]''. Its description in the [[Warcraft II: Tides of Darkness manual|''Tides of Darkness'' game manual]] reads: ''"Magiks involving the cardinal elements of the universe are favorites of the Mages. The Fireball is launched from the palms of the Mage and streaks like a comet blazing across the battlefield - slamming its fiery bulk into whatever stands in its path."''
**An [[Fireball (Heroes of Azeroth)|uncommon mage ability]] in the ''[[Trading Card Game]]''.
**A {{hs|Fireball|basic mage spell}} in ''[[Hearthstone (game)|Hearthstone]]''. Its flavor text reads: ''"This spell is useful for burning things. If you're looking for spells that toast things, or just warm them a little, you're in the wrong place."''

